4. CHANGES AND BUG REPORTS

Black Arrow maintains the Software. Changes to it are made by Black Arrow.

If you find a bug, want a feature, or need something to work differently, open
an issue on the project repository:

    https://github.com/morvoso/mindos/issues

That is the way to get the Software updated. Issues are read and acted on
there; patches sent by other routes, and forks published elsewhere, are not
part of this project.

If you do send Black Arrow a contribution — a patch, a suggestion, a fix in an
issue — you grant Black Arrow a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable
licence to use it in the Software and to license it under these terms. You keep
your own copyright in what you wrote.


5. NO WARRANTY

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT.

MindOS is an operating system. It writes to disks, installs drivers, changes
kernel parameters, applies system updates, and lets a language model run
commands on your machine. Any of that can destroy data or leave a machine
unbootable. Back up anything you care about, and do not run MindOS on a machine
you cannot afford to lose.


